I don't normally write these, but since there has been some interest I
thought I'd post one.  I don't make records of my games, from what I
understand the tournament system didn't record it, and what notes I had I
deleted when I started the next game.  So I'm going from memory; if I
forget something or make a mistake, smile :).
theta-Wiz-Elf-Fem-Cha, pacifist foodless wishless, 25360

The goal was foodless pacifist.  This was not intended to be an
especially low scoring ascention; aside from dropping items at the high altar, I
made no attempt to keep the score low.  
Scoring for dungeon depth (49) and Oracle consultations comes to 25280. 
This leaves 80 points for use-id of 4 scrolls/potions/wands.  Again,
totally unintentionally low - I just don't use things I don't know what
are.
I start by scumming up a ring of slow digestion, and got a spellbook of
sleep and magic marker as well.  Only 14 intelligence though.
Exploring the early dungeon and mines I get multiple large shops and two
bones files.  I end up with a huge stash in Sokoban. highlights include
three bags of holding, an amulet of reflection (Sokoban prize), three
magic markers, and a magic lamp.  One of my spellbooks turns out to be
charm monster.
Returning to the mines, I get a magic whistle from the tool shop, which
I somehow missed the first time around.  Deeper in the mines I find a
polymorph trap.  I make a golden naga, baby blue dragon, and a few less
impressive pets.  I finsih mine's end, and fall down a trap door into the
Gnome King's sub-basement.
Normally there is no Gnome King's sub-basement in NetHack.  Last year in
devnull, there was the Grue level which you could reach via stairs in
mine's end.  This year, you get there via portal from mine's end.  But
there's still another level below mine's end, just no stairs to reach it. 
It has upstairs leading to mine's end, though.
Without my good pets, I look aroud a little for the stairs, but with a
mind flayer blocking a narrow passage, I leave with a cursed scroll of
teleportation.  At some point I buy nine points of protection and two
Oracle consultations.  I tried to buy clairvoyance, but I accidentally let
my pets kill the priest.
Eventually I reach level 20, which is a bones file.  It's the player's
stash level.  I get dragon scale mail and a chest with a whole lot of
loot, next to an altar.  I explore as far as Medusa, finding a succubus and
a sink (no other foocubi or sinks in the dungeon).  I get two levels
from one and none from the other, putting me at level five.  Normally I'd
use wraith corpses, but I want to be foodless, and I don't have enough
potions to get all the way to 14.
I write a spellbook of polymorph and some time later (and with a little
alchemic luck) I get my potions as well as all the rings I need.  I
tried polying tools for a stethoscope and magic markers, without success. 
The foocubi didn't give me enough alignment so I reverse genocide
unicorns.  I also get crowned, expecting Stormbringer (oops :) ).
I do the quest, stealing the eye from the Dark One as a succubus.  Turns
out my pets could defeat him easily, which I discover when I bring him
to the quest home level as I level teleport out.  From there it's smooth
sailing until the ascention run.  I don't need anything from the wand,
so I ignore the castle entirely, going wishless.  I abandon my pets and
charm minotaurs to attack with as needed.  I steal the Candelabrum from
Vlad and the Book from the Wizard, waking him.
I level teleport to just below Asmodeus, go up, and once he's awake
level teleport to the vibrating square.  I perform the invocation and let
Asmodeus, the Wizard, and the Wizard's clone go get the Amulet for me. 
What's supposed to happen is that once they kill the High Priest, they
fight each other for the amulet, Asmodeus wins, and I steal the amulet from
Asmodeus.  But Asmodeus was being very slow at killing the Wizards, and
the Wizards were very interested in attacking me.
I try to kill the Wizards of Yendor by reverse genociding black dragons.
 Unfortunately, the disintegration blasts keep missing them, only
taking out a few summoned nasties.  I charm monster trying to nullify a
summoned A, which works, also getting me a pet black dragon.  One Wizard dies
and a (the pet?) black dragon picks up an amulet.  The Wizard summons a
replacement clone, they kill the black dragon, and I polymorph to a
succubus and steal the amulet.
I verify that it is the real amulet, and leave the sanctum.  As soon as
I leave I'm surrounded by the two Wizards, Asmodeus, Demogorgon (who
apparently just arrived), a captain, and a couple other monsters.  A Wizard
steals the amulet and Demogorgon makes me sick.  Elbereth, steal back
the amulet, teleport to upstairs, leave.
With just the two Wizards after me, I paralyze them and leave them
behind.  The Wizard makes another appearance on the way up, but another
paralysis takes care of him.  On Earth, I use the last three potions on him,
and he doesn't appear afterwards.  With a ring of conflict, jumping, and
wands of teleportaion, the rest of the planes are trivial.  (though it
was nice of that player monster to zap a rider with a wand of death)
If I win lowest scored ascention with this one, that's nice, but it
really is a beatable score, so do challenge me for the trophy.  :)




